<QuestionLayout
  title="Can I use Traverse with Python?"
  description="Yes. Python can consume Traverse today through a standard-library subprocess call to the real traverse-cli capability-package execute command. There is no native Python SDK yet."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/questions/can-i-use-traverse-with-python.html"
  category="Use Cases"
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>Yes. Python can consume Traverse today. The honest path is small: use Python's standard-library <code>subprocess</code> module to call the <code>traverse-cli</code> binary. There is no native Python SDK yet.</p>

  <h2>Call the real CLI command</h2>
  <p>The command for executing a checked-in capability package is <code>capability-package execute</code>. A minimal call looks like this:</p>

  <pre><code>import subprocess
from pathlib import Path

root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
manifest = root / "examples/capabilities/expedition-intent-agent/manifest.json"
request = root / "examples/capabilities/runtime-requests/interpret-expedition-intent.json"

subprocess.run(
    ["traverse-cli", "capability-package", "execute", str(manifest), str(request)],
    cwd=root,
    check=True,
)</code></pre>

  <p>That is a subprocess integration, not an embedded Python runtime. The CLI validates the package and executes the capability, while Python remains responsible for your application flow and data handling.</p>

  <h2>Use the checked-in example</h2>
  <p>The <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/tree/main/examples/consume-python" target="_blank" rel="noopener">consume-python example</a> is the reference path. It uses only the Python standard library, resolves an installed <code>traverse-cli</code> (or falls back to Cargo), and invokes the same <code>capability-package execute</code> command against the expedition fixtures. It landed in <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/pull/1416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">traverse#1416</a>, following <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1362" target="_blank" rel="noopener">traverse#1362</a>.</p>

  <h2>What is not available yet</h2>
  <p>There is no Python package that embeds the Traverse runtime, so this page does not pretend there is one. If you need a tighter integration, the current options are to keep the CLI process boundary or use the runtime's supported host integrations from another language.</p>

  <p>For the JavaScript and TypeScript path, see the <a href="/docs/guides/react-integration.html">React integration guide</a>. For the broader Rust question, see <a href="/questions/do-i-need-rust.html">Do I need to know Rust?</a>.</p>
</QuestionLayout>
